{"name":"False Morel","hex":"#784d4c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"false morel","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several Ascomycota mushrooms in the genus Gyromitra which bear a resemblance to the highly regarded true morels of the genus Morchella."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/false_morel"}],"entries":[{"title":"False morel","blocks":[{"text":"The name false morel is given to several species of mushroom which bear a resemblance to the highly regarded true morels of the genus Morchella. Like Morchella, false morels are members of the Pezizales, but within that group represent several unrelated taxa scattered through the families Morchellaceae, Discinaceae, and Helvellaceae, with the epithet \"false morel\" most often ascribed to members of the genus Gyromitra."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Gyromitra_Colima.jpg/330px-Gyromitra_Colima.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/False_morel","wikidata":"Q4501815"},{"title":"Gyromitra esculenta","blocks":[{"text":"Gyromitra esculenta is an ascomycete fungus from the genus Gyromitra. The fruiting body, or mushroom, is an irregular brain-shaped cap, dark brown in colour, that can reach 10 centimetres high and 15 cm (6 in) wide, perched on a stout white stipe up to 6 cm high. It is widely distributed across Europe and North America, normally fruiting in sandy soils under coniferous trees in spring and early summer."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/97/Fr%C3%BChjahrslorchel.JPG/330px-Fr%C3%BChjahrslorchel.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gyromitra_esculenta","wikidata":"Q900804"},{"title":"Morchella","blocks":[{"text":"Morchella, the true morels, is a genus of edible sac fungi closely related to anatomically simpler cup fungi in the order Pezizales. These distinctive fungi have a honeycomb appearance due to the network of ridges with pits composing their caps."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Morchella_conica_1_beentree.jpg/330px-Morchella_conica_1_beentree.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morchella","wikidata":"Q371101"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/2007-04-02_Gyromitra_esculenta_cropped.jpg/500px-2007-04-02_Gyromitra_esculenta_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/2007-04-02_Gyromitra_esculenta_cropped.jpg/500px-2007-04-02_Gyromitra_esculenta_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A younger specimen with a less wrinkled cap","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3A2007-04-02_Gyromitra_esculenta_cropped.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg/500px-False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg/1280px-False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg/500px-False_morels_for_sale_-_don%27t_touch.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"For sale with warning sign, Market Square, Helsinki","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFalse_morels_for_sale_-_don't_touch.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/83/Methylhydrazine-3D-balls.png/500px-Methylhydrazine-3D-balls.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_ca